OTP Verification Bypass via Response Handling
Vulnerability Type
Email OTP Verification / Authentication Workflow Issue

Summary
During TaskBear registration testing, Burp Suite captured 201 Created responses for OTP submissions, including an incorrect OTP (123456). The registration process proceeded to the next step. Server-side OTP validation still requires confirmation.

Vulnerable Endpoint
POST https://[REDACTED_API_HOST]/api/v1/uwa/auth/otp/verify

Steps to Reproduce
Open the TaskBear registration page and start registration using a temporary email address.
Submit the OTP and capture the verification request and successful response using Burp Suite.
Start a new registration using another controlled email address and proceed to the OTP verification page.
Submit an incorrect OTP (123456) and capture the verification request and response in Burp Suite.
Compare the captured responses and inspect the verification status and response body. Document any response manipulation performed during authorized testing.
Forward the response and observe whether the application proceeds to the registration details page and subsequent onboarding process.
Payload / Response Observed
The captured response contained the following structure:

HTTP/2 201 Created
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
X-Powered-By: Express
X-Ratelimit-Limit: 10
X-Ratelimit-Remaining: 9

{
  "contact": "[REDACTED_EMAIL]",
  "verifiedAt": "[REDACTED_TIMESTAMP]"
}
